      "pins": ["D3 output", "J4.2", "J9.2", "servo-rail terminals of C1, C5, C6, C8"],
      "nets": ["D3 output / servo power rail", "GND"],
      "observed": "On schematic page 1, the output of D3 connects to the servo power rail and also runs directly down to a GND symbol. The rail supplies the servo headers and the capacitor bank.",
      "expected": "The servo power rail should be fed from +5V through D3 and be isolated from GND except through the bulk capacitors; the specification says the diode feeds a dedicated servo rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "D3 PMEG3030EP 3A 360mV; the output wire is connected to GND (page 1)."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "From +5V, a second diode D2 (PMEG3030EP, annotated \"3A 360mV\" in the schematic — a low-forward-voltage-drop Schottky) feeds a dedicated servo power rail backed by four 100 µF capacitors before reaching J3/J8 pin 2."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The external +5V rail is effectively shorted to ground through D3. This can cause the supply to current-limit or shut down, and may damage the diode or supply; the servos will not receive usable power.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic shows the output of the servo-supply diode connected directly to GND. This contradicts the specified isolated servo power rail and would short the supply when powered."
}

